From e118bb0824bc2d5f6a85f88d51ead1c458c51229 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guan Xuetao <gxt@pku.edu.cn>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:31:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] DADAO: Add minimal target skeleton with MC support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the minimal DADAO target directory structure under
llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/:

- CMakeLists.txt: Component group + TargetInfo/MCTargetDesc subdirs
- DADAO.h: Minimal header (stub)
- DADAOTargetMachine.{h,cpp}: Minimal TargetMachine (not built by MC-only
  build, but present for completeness)
- TargetInfo/DADAOTargetInfo.{h,cpp}: RegisterTarget with triple 'dadao',
  description 'DADAO SimRISC'
- MCTargetDesc/DADAOMCTargetDesc.{h,cpp}: MC-level registration:
  RegisterMCAsmInfo, RegisterMCInstPrinter, RegisterELFStreamer
- MCTargetDesc/DADAOMCAsmInfo.{h,cpp}: MCAsmInfoELF subclass,
  IsLittleEndian=false (big endian), CommentString='#'
- MCTargetDesc/DADAOELFObjectWriter.cpp: MCELFObjectTargetWriter stub,
  EM_DADAO=0x0DA0 (contract-elf.md §1.1), getRelocType() stub
- MCInstPrinter stub: Required by llvm-mc at runtime to avoid crash

No instructions, registers, or .td files are defined (out of scope).
No CodeGen (tablegen) dependencies.
